  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A Nightshelf lector of the Great Thaw era, allied with Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute, a crystalline-weaver and negotiator of considerable influence. ☽'Ilsancuia is best understood through three facts: they spent a decade restoring an artifact they believed was in pain, they died engineering the collapse that sealed the deep-passages during the Orca Incursion, and the memorial raised where they fell does not bear their name.
    
    ## The Medallion and Its Keeper
    
    ☽'Ilsancuia discovered the Thaw-Paths Medallion — a palm-sized aurora-glass disc carved with pathways that glow under starlight — in the abandoned nest of ☽'Iarlocias the Silent, a predecessor whose reasons for sealing it away became clear only later. Beside the Medallion lay a fire-core hammer, cracked but still warm, propped against the wall as though its owner intended to return. ☽'Ilsancuia took both.
    
    They tracked ☽'Iarlocias to the upper warrens near ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~, a deep Nightshelf settlement, and were warned to cease restoring the Medallion. They did not. The restoration consumed a decade, driven by ☽'Ilsancuia's conviction that the Medallion was *suffering* — a claim the chronicle account from "The Medallion's Paths of Ice" supports with descriptions of intensifying glow and destabilizing effects on the surrounding ice. That same chronicle records ☽'Ilsancuia dying while communing with the artifact, which sits uneasily against the consistent account — preserved across every other source — that they died in an engineered tunnel collapse during the Orca Incursion. Both may describe the same event differently. Neither is without corroboration.
    
    ## Character and Associations
    
    ☽'Ilsancuia learned Shawl☽ Sun — the fire-memory magic drawn from the Dreaming Tooth — late in life, and bore the burn scars permanently because they refused to stop working through the healing. The Augur once attempted to tend these wounds; ☽'Ilsancuia withdrew without explanation. They spoke in the elliptical manner of deep-dwellers and never looked directly at the Augur when offering counsel. Whether this constituted courtesy or refusal remains unresolved.
    
    They served as patron of ☽'ofund' Guild, a Nightshelf trading house, from its founding season. Their endorsement on Guild broadsheets carried commercial weight long after their death.
    
    ## Death and Legacy
    
    During the Orca Incursion, when salt-water and raiders flooded the deep-passages, ☽'Ilsancuia restored the Medallion's pathways a final time — not to escape, but to seal the tunnels behind the retreating population. The collapse they engineered killed them. The cracked hammer was still in their grip.
    
    Signum∴men, the Nightshelf memorial tradition, marks the site. No name appears; custom forbids it. Lectors who pass leave fire-cores at its base. ☽'Ilsancuia's ice-pick survived the collapse and is carried as Signum∴men weight — an obligatory burden on routes where every ounce matters, because you do not set down a relic of the dead.
