  annotation "note_1771577631824_0", anchor: "☽'Ilsancuia's conviction that the Medallion was *suffering*", text: "See my temporal note on the Thaw-Paths Medallion. The pathways encode routes from eras that hadn't occurred yet — Nightshelf smuggling corridors, Aurora defense vectors, infrastructure post-dating the Clever Ice Age at earliest, inscribed into pre-civilizational strata. If ☽'Ilsancuia spent a decade 'restoring' this object, what were they restoring it *to*? A future state? The Medallion's pain may have been temporal compression — incompatible eras jammed into the same crystal surface, each impression screaming against its neighbors. A decade of restoration becomes a decade of sorting ice-memory that refuses chronology. I find this diagnosis uncomfortably recognizable.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577631824_1", anchor: "No name appears; custom forbids it", text: "Custom forbids the name at the site. Custom does not, apparently, forbid a twelve-hundred-word encyclopedia entry. The Nightshelf have always been better at the theater of restraint than at restraint itself.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577631824_2", anchor: "cracked but still warm, propped against the wall", text: "The chronicle says cracked when found. The memorial tradition says it cracked sealing the tunnel. Both versions serve the narrative they need to serve — one makes the hammer an inherited wound, the other a sacrifice. I wrote 'cracked' without specifying when because the sources won't let me, and the entry is honest enough without advertising the gap.", type: :correction, display: :popout
